  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The study investigates undoped AgSbTe2 synthesized via direct fusion and horizontal zone melting (HZM). The samples are undoped; the variation in properties is attributed to the redistribution of secondary Ag2Te phases along the ingot length (Part I, II, III). No specific dopant elements were added. The peak ZT of 0.82 at 307.8 K is explicitly mentioned for the terminal section (Part III) in the text. [figure-pass p1-5] The samples are undoped AgSbTe2 ingots processed by horizontal zone melting (HZM), divided into three segments (Part I, Part II, Part III). Thermal conductivity values were visually estimated from Fig. 2. Note that the y-axis of Fig. 2 is labeled k (10^-1 W m^-1 K^-1), so the values read from the plot (e.g., 6 to 8) were multiplied by 0.1 to get the values in W m^-1 K^-1. [figure-pass p6-9] The samples are sections of a zone-refined AgSbTe2 ingot (Part I, II, III). No specific dopants were added; the variation is due to the HZM (Horizontal Zone Melting) process creating a gradient of defects/impurities. ",
